                <pb facs="1005" n="891" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg891"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.51/222: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Salvador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hewes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-12-30T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 30,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>53. Reference your December 28, noon.</p>
                <p>To what terms do you refer? Is Mr. Keith proceeding under contract of last June
                    or under new contract of December 1st?</p>
                <p>Because of new provisions in December contract, Department is still considering
                    advisability of acquiescing in contract and has not as yet committed itself to a
                    further exchange of notes. Also it is not prepared at this time to approve of
                    Mr. Keith proceeding under contract of last June. Bearing this in mind, you will
                    refrain from discussing loan with Government officials. If you are asked
                    regarding Department’s views you should simply say that matter is still
                    receiving consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
